.TH SOULLESS\-LAUNCHER 1 "July 2026" "soulless\-launcher 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
soulless\-launcher \- command\-center launcher for the COSMIC desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soulless\-launcher
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.br
.B soulless\-launcher
.BR \-h | \-\-help
.br
.B soulless\-launcher
.BR \-V | \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B soulless\-launcher
is a launcher for the COSMIC desktop environment. It provides universal search
across applications, files, command\-line tools, Steam games, Flatpaks and
AppImages; user\-defined drawers with drag\-and\-drop; an encrypted vault; and live
system monitors.
.PP
With no arguments it runs as a resident daemon. It is normally started at login
from
.I /etc/xdg/autostart
and stays warm for the session, showing and hiding its
.BR wlr\-layer\-shell (7)
surface on request rather than starting a fresh process each time. A companion
COSMIC panel applet,
.BR soulless\-applet ,
activates it over D\-Bus.
.PP
Because the autostart entry is converted to a systemd user unit when the user
manager starts, a
.B full reboot
is required after installation \- logging out and back in does not re\-scan
.IR /etc/xdg/autostart .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B toggle
Show the launcher if it is hidden, hide it if it is visible. The command is
routed over D\-Bus to the running daemon; it does not start a second instance.
If no daemon is running, one is started.
.IP
Note that running
.B toggle
from a terminal will only ever
.I show
the launcher: typing gives the terminal keyboard focus, which triggers the
launcher's click\-away dismiss, so there is never a visible surface left to hide.
The hide branch is reached from a keybind or script that does not steal focus.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary to standard output and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information to standard output and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/soulless/config.ron
Main configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/soulless/theme.ron
Colour overrides. Any subset of the theme's colour tokens may be given as hex
values; unspecified tokens keep their defaults.
.TP
.I ~/.config/soulless/backgrounds/
Right\-panel background images. The first image alphabetically is used.
Portrait orientation, roughly 460x1100 pixels or larger.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/soulless/drawers.json
Saved drawer contents and layout.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/soulless/
Index caches. Safe to delete; they are rebuilt on next launch.
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/autostart/com.github.hmrdsmoke.soulless\-launcher.desktop
Autostart entry that starts the daemon at login.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Tracing filter. Defaults to
.BR warn .
Set to
.B info
or
.B debug
for diagnostics.
.TP
.B COSMIC_SINGLE_INSTANCE
Set to
.B false
or
.B 0
to disable single\-instance behaviour and force a new process. Intended for
debugging.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including
.B \-\-help
and
.BR \-\-version .
.TP
.B 1
An unrecognized argument was given.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Toggle the launcher from a keybind:
.B soulless\-launcher toggle
.TP
Run in the foreground with diagnostics:
.B RUST_LOG=info soulless\-launcher
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR soulless\-applet (1),
.BR busctl (1)
.PP
